es. To maximize the chance of forming additional melds, it's best to discard a tile that is not part of any potential meld. T1 is a terminal tile not involved in any existing or potential melds and is the last one available, making it a safe discard.\\nReason: Discarding T1 preserves the possibility of forming a Chow with W4-5-6 if W5 is drawn, while removing a tile that doesn't contribute to any high-scoring patterns. The last T1 in the wall ensures no other player can claim it for a meld.\\nAnswer: Play T1\"}"}
